.TH WERKMEISTER-FEATURE-SERVICES 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-feature\-services \- List services and their endpoints for a feature
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister feature services\fR <feature>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Shows each service of a running feature with its source and endpoint:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
=== Services for: my\-feature ===

  Service                    Source    Endpoint                        Type           
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  backend                    k8s      localhost:9052                  api
  frontend                   local    localhost:11101                 web
  search                     baseline  localhost:11102                 api

  local = running in Docker on this machine  |  baseline = services.yaml baseline_upstream  |  k8s = port\-forwarded from k8s cluster
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBSource\fR is \fBlocal\fR for a container running on this machine, \fBbaseline\fR for the \fBbaseline_upstream\fR named in \fBservices.yaml\fR, \fBk8s\fR for a port\-forward from the cluster, and \fBN/A\fR when the service has no endpoint (\fB(not configured)\fR). If the feature isn't running, the command says so and prints \fBwerkmeister feature up <feature>\fR instead of failing.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
